.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/worktrees/
.codex
.idea/

# Ansible's per-project scratch directory (`.ansible/`, holding an empty
# `.lock`), which ansible tooling creates at the working directory when a gate
# or test runs it. Never durable state. Unignored, a factory engine checkpoint
# committed it inside the sandbox clone, so the clone differed from the
# published pull-request head and proof_verify could name no single publish
# head. proof_grade then failed closed three times (livespec-dev-tooling-h2i4u2,
# run 01M70ETFK3ZT, 2026-11-09). Unanchored, because the path follows the cwd.
.ansible/

# Playwright MCP browser-tool scratch (page snapshots, console logs) —
# per-session, never durable state.
.playwright-mcp/

# Stray embedded-Dolt store written by the EXTERNAL beads `bd` binary (upstream
# code reached through the livespec-orchestrator-beads-fabro tenant — nothing in
# this repository creates one). It appears at the PROCESS CWD carrying the name
# `.beads/.gitignore` already anticipates INSIDE `.beads/`: the right name in the
# wrong parent, so the path is cwd-resolved rather than beads-home-resolved. Not
# a fallback ignoring `dolt.mode: server` — the store is INERT (`repo_state.json`
# carries `"branches":{}`) while ledger reads went on being served by the
# configured 127.0.0.1:3307 tenant. An ignore file cannot reach a sibling of its
# own directory, which is why the root needs this rule — and why the rule is
# UNANCHORED: a cwd-resolved path follows whatever directory `bd` ran from.
# See livespec-dev-tooling-to6hh2.
embeddeddolt/

### Python toolchain artifacts
# Note: .mypy_cache/ is intentionally NOT listed. Mypy is not used
# (livespec-dev-tooling pins pyright); its cache path is therefore
# not a tolerated artifact.
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
.coverage.*
# check-per-file-coverage's provenance marker for check-coverage's consume-once reuse
.livespec-coverage-reuse-token
# check-per-file-coverage's failed-suite receipt for check-coverage's consume-once verdict reuse
.livespec-coverage-failure-receipt
.ruff_cache/
.pyright/
.mutmut-cache/
mutants/
htmlcov/

